question:
are the following configurations set at the host level of cloud containers:
- minimal set of file system permissions required;
- containers should not mount local file systems on a host;
- any file changes that containers need to persist to disk should be made within storage volumes specifically allocated for this purpose;
- containers should not be able to mount sensitive directories on a host’s file system, especially those containing configuration settings for the operating system;
- use tools to monitor which directories are mounted by containers and prevent these containers from being deployed;

