question:
does the cloud provider that processes personal data on behalf of have to sign a contract that includes the following terms as a minimum?
- only act on the written instructions of the client;
- ensure that people processing the data are subject to a duty of confidence;
- take appropriate measures to ensure the security of processing;
- only engage sub-processors with the prior consent of and under a written contract;
- assist client in providing subject access and allowing data subjects to exercise their rights under the gdpr;
- assist in meeting its gdpr obligations in relation to the security of processing, the notification of personal data breaches, and data protection impact assessments;
- delete or return all personal data as requested at the end of the contract; and
- submit to audits and inspections, provide whatever information it needs to ensure that they are both meeting their article 28 obligations, and tell immediately if it is asked to do something infringing the gdpr or other data protection law of the eu or a member state.

